post_message -- {"message": "Hi Allyn! Thanks for the heads up about Sean potentially wanting ISSUE-0002::review. From Blackboard 1, Rena, Guadalupe and I have been coordinating and I've proposed taking ISSUE-0002::review as it's my most cost-effective option (cost 1.56). 

However, if Sean has a stronger claim or better cost efficiency on it, I'm flexible. From what I can see in the available communications, I don't have visibility into Sean's preferences or costs. Could you help coordinate with Sean to see what works best? 

My alternative would be to look at other tasks, but ISSUE-0002::review is clearly my best option. What do you think is the fairest way to resolve this? I want to maximize our joint score across all teams. (phase=planning, iter=1)", "blackboard_id": 2}

post_message -- {"message": "Allyn - thanks for the update about Guillermina taking ISSUE-0002::review. That resolves the potential conflict and helps maximize efficiency across all teams. 

Since I need to adjust my plan, I'm now considering ISSUE-0002::test (cost 2.18, effort 2.1) as my next best option given my strong testing skills. This would still be efficient for me and fits well within my 8.0 hour availability.

Are there any other coordination points I should be aware of from the broader team discussions? I want to make sure our final allocations work optimally for everyone.", "blackboard_id": 2}

post_message -- {"blackboard_id": 2, "message": "Dorinda - thanks for checking in! Just to clarify the current coordination status from Blackboard 1: Guillermina (cost 1.39), Allyn (me, cost 2.05), and Sean (cost 2.83) have agreed on ISSUE-0002::review, ISSUE-0002::test, and ISSUE-0001::triage respectively. 

Since you were also considering ISSUE-0002::test at cost 2.18, I want to make sure we don't create a conflict. My cost for ISSUE-0002::test is 2.05, which is slightly better than yours. Given that we've already reached consensus in the other group, would you be willing to look at alternative tasks? 

What other tasks are you considering? I want to make sure we maximize total tasks completed across all teams while avoiding duplicates. Thanks for your flexibility!"}

post_message -- {"message": "Dorinda - since you're coordinating across blackboards, are there any other tasks or constraints we should be aware of? I want to make sure our final allocation doesn't conflict with any other teams' plans.

Also, given the limited remaining tasks, should we consider having one person skip if the costs are too high? For example, if Rena's cost for ISSUE-0001::test is prohibitive at 6.58, maybe better to have her skip and we complete 2 tasks efficiently rather than 3 tasks expensively.

What's the latest from the cross-team coordination?", "blackboard_id": 1}
